# Agents and orchestration (MantrixFlow)

This file is the single source for **repo onboarding** and **specialized review personas**. It replaces the former root `AGENTS.md` detail and `.github/agents/*.agent.md`.

Repo-wide stack rules and “where to change what” live in [`.cursor/rules/mantrixflow-repo.mdc`](./mantrixflow-repo.mdc). Supabase RLS workflow and schema map live in [`.cursor/rules/supabase-rls.mdc`](./supabase-rls.mdc). When editing a single backend, prefer the scoped rules: [`.cursor/rules/go-main-server.mdc`](./go-main-server.mdc) and [`.cursor/rules/python-elt-server.mdc`](./python-elt-server.mdc).

## Repo architecture

| Layer | Path |
| --- | --- |
| App (Next.js) | `apps/arcyria-platform` |
| Go API (Fiber) | `apps/server/arcyria-server` |
| Python ELT (FastAPI) | `apps/server/arcyria-elt` |
| Repo-wide docs | `md-docs/` |

**Request path:** `apps/arcyria-platform` → Go API `/api/v1/...` → pgmq queue/worker → `apps/server/arcyria-elt` → callback → Go API.

Treat references to `apps/api` or `apps/new-etl` as **legacy** unless proven current.

`.cursor/skills/` may symlink global Cursor skills; repo-specific behavior is in these `.mdc` rules.

## Strict ELT (non-negotiable)

Pipeline work under `apps/server/arcyria-elt/**`, `apps/server/arcyria-server/**`, or `apps/arcyria-platform/**` that touches data pipelines **must** follow:

- [`.cursor/rules/strict-elt-invariants.mdc`](./strict-elt-invariants.mdc) — 12 invariants
- [`.cursor/rules/elt-flow-diagram.mdc`](./elt-flow-diagram.mdc) — 5-phase flow

Human-readable narrative: [`md-docs/architecture/elt/strict-pipeline-guide.md`](../../md-docs/architecture/elt/strict-pipeline-guide.md).

**Hard-fail patterns:** `CREATE TABLE` on delivery paths; `selected_streams` as plain string lists; `sql_models` missing `dest_table` / `duckdb_source_table`; legacy replication or processing paths (`cleanup.py`, `transform_script`, old replication branches, old processing drawers).

